/-!
# The twisted hat complex after adding a basepoint: the Koszul factor `1 + t`

Adding a basepoint to a Heegaard diagram in a region `R₀` that already contains one
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepoint`) tensors the hat complex with the two-dimensional
space `W` on the two new points `p` and `q`, with zero differential
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatDifferential_comp_addBasepointChainEquiv`): the two crescents
`C_α` and `C_β` are the domains from `p` to `q`, and they cancel modulo two. The new diagram also
has one new periodic domain, `C_α - C_β`, the class of the sphere around the new basepoint
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv`). With twisted coefficients
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential`) the two crescents no longer cancel: their
labels differ by this class, so the twisted complex of the new diagram is the twisted complex of the
old one, with coefficients pushed into the larger group ring, tensored with the Koszul complex

`p ↦ (1 + t) q`, `q ↦ 0`

of the monomial `t = t^{C_α - C_β}`. This is the Koszul factor of the auxiliary `S¹ × S²` summand in
the twisted comparison for diagrams with several basepoints: a diagram of `Y` with `b` basepoints
has the periodic domains of `Y # (b - 1) (S¹ × S²)`, and each added basepoint contributes one Koszul
factor `1 + t_i`.

**Coefficients.** The group ring `R'` of the periodic domains of the new diagram contains the group
ring `R` of the old ones through the ring map
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRingHom` induced by `Q ↦ (Q, 0)` under
`addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv`. Since `R₀` contains a basepoint, every old periodic domain
vanishes on `R₀`, and `(Q, 0)` is just `Q` extended by zero over the new regions.

**Reference domains.** Reference domains `D_x` of the old diagram induce reference domains of the
new one (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.ReferenceDomains.addBasepoint`): the reference generator of
`(x, k)` is `(x₀, p)` for the reference generator `x₀` of `x`, with reference domain `D_x` at
`(x, p)` and `D_x + C_β` at `(x, q)`. With these choices:

* between generators with the same new point, the counted domains are the old ones extended by zero,
  with the same labels, so the twisted coefficient is the image of the old one
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_self`);
* no domain is counted from `q` to `p`
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_one_zero`);
* from `(x, p)` to `(y, q)` the counted domains are a nonnegative domain `E` of Maslov index zero
  from `x` to `y` avoiding the basepoints together with one crescent. When `E = 0` is the only such
  domain, the twisted coefficient is `1 + t` for `x = y` and `0` otherwise: the crescent `C_β` has
  label `0` and the crescent `C_α` has label `C_α - C_β`
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_of_ne`).

So, when the zero domain is the only nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero to `y` avoiding the
basepoints, the twisted hat differential of the new diagram at `y` is
`(∂' c)(y, k) = ∑ₓ c(x, k) ι(c(x, y)) + [k = q] (1 + t) c(y, p)`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply`), the tensor product of
the old twisted differential with the Koszul complex of `1 + t`. Under the augmentation `t ↦ 1` the
factor `1 + t` becomes `0`, recovering `∂ ⊗ 1` on `CF̂ ⊗ W` at the level of chains. This is a
chain-level comparison only: homology does not commute with the non-flat augmentation.

**Homology.** The Koszul factor does not change the twisted homology. The ring map
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRetraction` `ε : R' → R`, induced by
`(Q, m) ↦ Q`, sets `t` to `1` and is a left inverse of `ι`, and its kernel is generated by `1 + t`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.ker_addBasepointTwistedRetraction`). The new complex is the mapping
cone of multiplication by `1 + t` on the old complex with coefficients in `R'`, and `1 + t` is not a
zero divisor, so the cone computes the homology of the quotient by `1 + t`, which `ε` identifies
with the old complex. Concretely, the projection `c ↦ (y ↦ ε (c(y, q)))`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedProjection`) is a chain map, semilinear along
`ε`. Under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply` (`R₀` contains a
basepoint, and the zero domain is the only nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero between two
generators avoiding the basepoints), when the old twisted differential also squares to zero the
projection induces a bijection on homology
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_bijective`). So, under
these hypotheses, the twisted homology of the new diagram is that of the old one, with `R'` acting
through `ε` (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv`,
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_smul`); in particular `1 + t`
annihilates it. This is the twisted comparison for an auxiliary `S¹ × S²` summand: each added
basepoint contributes a Koszul factor `1 + tᵢ`, on which the coefficients act through the
augmentation of that factor. The vanishing of the square of the twisted differential is a
hypothesis, as it is not proved for the incidence data in general.

The genus-one diagram of a lens space with an added basepoint, in particular the twice-pointed
diagram of `S³`, is treated in `TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.Twisted.LensSpace`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRingHom`: the ring map `R → R'` of group rings of
  periodic domains.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.ReferenceDomains.addBasepoint`: the induced reference domains.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRetraction`: the ring map `R' → R` setting
  `t` to `1`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedProjection`: the chain map
  `c ↦ (y ↦ ε (c(y, q)))` from the new twisted complex to the old one.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv`: the induced identification of
  twisted homologies.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_self`,
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_one_zero`,
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_of_ne`: the twisted
  coefficients of the diagram with an added basepoint.
* `HeegaardRegionSystem.WeaklyAdmissibleAt.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self`: the
  coefficient `1 + t` at a generator where the diagram is weakly admissible.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply`: its twisted hat
  differential is the old one tensored with the Koszul complex of `1 + t`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.ker_addBasepointTwistedRetraction`: the kernel of `ε` is generated
  by `1 + t`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero`: the new
  twisted differential squares to zero if the old one does.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_bijective`: the projection
  induces a bijection on twisted homology.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_smul` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepoint_one_add_single_smul_eq_zero`: the coefficients act on
  the new twisted homology through `ε`, so `1 + t` acts by zero.

## References

* P. Ozsváth, A. Stipsicz and Z. Szabó, *Combinatorial Heegaard Floer homology and nice Heegaard
  diagrams*, Adv. Math. **231** (2012), [arXiv:0912.0830](https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0830), §10
  (twisted coefficients for diagrams with several basepoints, and the comparison with the singly
  pointed theory).
* P. Ozsváth and Z. Szabó, *Holomorphic disks and three-manifold invariants: properties and
  applications*, Ann. of Math. **159** (2004),
  [arXiv:math/0105202](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105202), §8 (Floer homology with twisted
  coefficients, and the twisted Floer homology of `S¹ × S²`).
-/

public section

open MonoidAlgebra Function

namespace TauCeti

namespace HeegaardRegionSystem

universe u v w

variable {n : ℕ} {Point : Type u} {Region : Type v} {Basepoint : Type w}
  (H : HeegaardRegionSystem n Point Region Basepoint) (r₀ : Region)

section Ring

/-- The ring map from the group ring of the periodic domains of a diagram to that of the diagram
with an added basepoint in `r₀`, induced by the inclusion `Q ↦ (Q, 0)` of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv`. -/
noncomputable def addBasepointTwistedRingHom :
    MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative H.periodicDomains) →+*
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains) :=
  mapDomainRingHom (ZMod 2) (AddMonoidHom.toMultiplicative
    ((H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀).toAddMonoidHom.comp (AddMonoidHom.inl _ _)))

/-- The ring map sends the monomial `t^Q` to the monomial `t^{(Q, 0)}`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedRingHom_single (Q : H.periodicDomains) (a : ZMod 2) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (single (Multiplicative.ofAdd Q) a) =
      single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (Q, 0))) a := by
  simp [addBasepointTwistedRingHom]

end Ring

namespace ReferenceDomains

variable {H r₀}

/-- The reference domains of the diagram with an added basepoint in a region `r₀` containing a
basepoint, induced by reference domains `D_x` of the original diagram: the reference generator of
`(x, k)` is `(x₀, 0)` for the reference generator `x₀` of `x`, and its reference domain is `D_x`
extended by `k` on the `β`-crescent and by zero on the other new regions. -/
noncomputable def addBasepoint (r : H.ReferenceDomains) (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).ReferenceDomains where
  base g := H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ (r.base ((H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).symm g).1) 0
  domain g := Sum.elim (r.domain ((H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).symm g).1)
    ![0, (((H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).symm g).2 : ℤ), 0]
  isDomainBetween_domain g := by
    obtain ⟨⟨x, k⟩, rfl⟩ := (H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).surjective g
    obtain ⟨z₀, rfl⟩ := hr₀
    simp only [addBasepointGeneratorEquiv_apply, addBasepointGeneratorEquiv_symm_apply]
    rw [isDomainBetween_addBasepoint_iff]
    exact ⟨r.isDomainBetween_domain x, by simp [r.domain_basepoint]⟩
  domain_basepoint g z := by
    rcases z with z | z <;> simp [r.domain_basepoint]
  base_eq_base {g g' D} hD hz := by
    obtain ⟨⟨x, i⟩, rfl⟩ := (H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).surjective g
    obtain ⟨⟨y, j⟩, rfl⟩ := (H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).surjective g'
    simp only [addBasepointGeneratorEquiv_apply, addBasepointGeneratorEquiv_symm_apply] at hD ⊢
    rw [isDomainBetween_addBasepoint_iff] at hD
    rw [r.base_eq_base hD.1 fun z => by simpa using hz (Sum.inl z)]

variable (r : H.ReferenceDomains) (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)

/-- The reference generator of `(x, k)` is `(x₀, 0)`, for the reference generator `x₀` of `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepoint_base (x : H.Generator) (k : Fin 2) :
    (r.addBasepoint hr₀).base (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k) =
      H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ (r.base x) 0 := by
  simp [addBasepoint]

/-- The reference domain of `(x, k)` is that of `x`, extended by `k` on the `β`-crescent and by
zero on the other new regions. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepoint_domain (x : H.Generator) (k : Fin 2) :
    (r.addBasepoint hr₀).domain (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k) =
      Sum.elim (r.domain x) ![0, (k : ℤ), 0] := by
  simp [addBasepoint]

/-- The label of a domain of the diagram with an added basepoint is the label of its restriction
to the old regions, extended by the multiplicities of the new regions corrected by the reference
domains. -/
theorem addBasepoint_label (x y : H.Generator) (i j : Fin 2) (D : Region ⊕ Fin 3 → ℤ) :
    (r.addBasepoint hr₀).label (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x i)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y j) D =
      Sum.elim (r.label x y (D ∘ Sum.inl))
        fun m => ![0, (i : ℤ), 0] m + D (Sum.inr m) - ![0, (j : ℤ), 0] m := by
  funext s
  rcases s with s | m <;>
    simp only [label_def, addBasepoint_domain, Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply, Sum.elim_inl,
      Sum.elim_inr, comp_apply]

end ReferenceDomains

section Hat

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region] {χ : Region → ℤ}
  {r : H.ReferenceDomains} {r₀} (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)

/-- **Twisted coefficients between generators with the same new point.** When `r₀` contains a
basepoint, the twisted coefficient of the diagram with an added basepoint from `(x, k)` to `(y, k)`
is the image of the twisted coefficient of the original diagram from `x` to `y`. -/
theorem twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_self (x y : H.Generator) (k : Fin 2) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y k) =
      H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) := by
  classical
  have hset := H.hatDomains_addBasepoint_self (χ := χ) r₀ hr₀ x y k
  have hinj : Injective fun D : Region → ℤ => (Sum.elim D 0 : Region ⊕ Fin 3 → ℤ) :=
    fun D E h => funext fun s => congrFun h (Sum.inl s)
  rcases (H.hatDomains χ x y).finite_or_infinite with hfin | hinf
  · have := hfin.fintype
    have : Fintype ((H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDomains (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y k)) :=
      (show Set.Finite _ by rw [hset]; exact hfin.image _).fintype
    rw [twistedHatCoefficient_eq_sum, twistedHatCoefficient_eq_sum, map_sum]
    have hmem (E : H.hatDomains χ x y) : (Sum.elim E.val 0 : Region ⊕ Fin 3 → ℤ) ∈
        (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDomains (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k)
          (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y k) := by
      rw [hset]
      exact ⟨E.val, E.property, rfl⟩
    refine (Fintype.sum_bijective (fun E => ⟨Sum.elim E.val 0, hmem E⟩)
      ⟨fun E F h => Subtype.ext (hinj (congrArg Subtype.val h)), fun D => ?_⟩ _ _
      fun E => ?_).symm
    · obtain ⟨E, hE, hDE⟩ := (Set.ext_iff.mp hset D.val).mp D.property
      exact ⟨⟨E, hE⟩, Subtype.ext hDE⟩
    · rw [addBasepointTwistedRingHom_single]
      congr 2
      refine Subtype.ext ?_
      dsimp only
      rw [H.coe_addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv_mk_zero r₀ hr₀,
        ReferenceDomains.addBasepoint_label]
      funext s
      rcases s with s | m
      · simp
      · fin_cases m <;> simp
  · rw [twistedHatCoefficient_of_infinite hinf, map_zero, twistedHatCoefficient_of_infinite]
    rw [hset]
    exact hinf.image hinj.injOn

/-- **No twisted coefficient from `q` to `p`.** When `r₀` contains a basepoint, the twisted
coefficient of the diagram with an added basepoint from `(x, 1)` to `(y, 0)` vanishes. -/
theorem twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_one_zero (x y : H.Generator) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0) = 0 :=
  twistedHatCoefficient_eq_zero_of_hatDomains_eq_empty
    (H.hatDomains_addBasepoint_one_zero r₀ hr₀ x y)

/-- Under the hypothesis that the zero domain is the only nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero
from `x` to `y` avoiding the basepoints, the set of such domains is `{0}` when `x = y` and empty
otherwise. -/
private theorem setOf_maslovIndex_eq_zero {x y : H.Generator}
    (h₀ : ∀ E, H.IsDomainBetween x y E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
      H.maslovIndex χ x y E = 0 → E = 0) (E : Region → ℤ) :
    E ∈ {E | H.IsDomainBetween x y E ∧ (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) ∧ 0 ≤ E ∧
      H.maslovIndex χ x y E = 0} ↔ x = y ∧ E = 0 := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hD, hz, hE₀, hμ⟩
    obtain rfl := h₀ E hD hz hE₀ hμ
    exact ⟨isDomainBetween_zero_iff.mp hD, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨rfl, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨isDomainBetween_zero x, fun z => rfl, le_rfl, map_zero _⟩

include hr₀ in
/-- Under the hypothesis that the zero domain is the only nonnegative periodic domain of Maslov
index zero at `x` avoiding the basepoints, the domains counted from `(x, 0)` to `(x, 1)` in the
diagram with an added basepoint are exactly the two crescents `C_β` and `C_α`. -/
private theorem hatDomains_addBasepoint_zero_one_self {x : H.Generator}
    (h₀ : ∀ E, H.IsDomainBetween x x E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
      H.maslovIndex χ x x E = 0 → E = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDomains (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) =
      {Sum.elim (0 : Region → ℤ) (Pi.single 1 1), Sum.elim (0 : Region → ℤ) (Pi.single 0 1)} := by
  ext D
  rw [H.hatDomains_addBasepoint_zero_one r₀ hr₀ x x]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨⟨E, k⟩, ⟨hE, -⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨-, rfl⟩ := (H.setOf_maslovIndex_eq_zero h₀ E).mp hE
    fin_cases k <;> simp
  · have h0 := (H.setOf_maslovIndex_eq_zero h₀ 0).mpr ⟨rfl, rfl⟩
    rintro (rfl | rfl)
    exacts [⟨(0, 1), ⟨h0, Set.mem_univ _⟩, rfl⟩, ⟨(0, 0), ⟨h0, Set.mem_univ _⟩, rfl⟩]

/-- **The Koszul coefficient `1 + t` from `p` to `q`.** Suppose that `r₀` contains a basepoint and
that the zero domain is the only nonnegative periodic domain of Maslov index zero at `x` avoiding
the basepoints. Then the twisted coefficient of the diagram with an added basepoint from `(x, 0)`
to `(x, 1)` is `1 + t`, for the monomial `t` of the periodic domain `C_α - C_β`: the crescent `C_α`
is counted with label `C_α - C_β` and the crescent `C_β` with label `0`. -/
theorem twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self {x : H.Generator}
    (h₀ : ∀ E, H.IsDomainBetween x x E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
      H.maslovIndex χ x x E = 0 → E = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) =
      1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1 := by
  have hne : (Sum.elim 0 (Pi.single 1 1) : Region ⊕ Fin 3 → ℤ) ≠
      Sum.elim (0 : Region → ℤ) (Pi.single 0 1) :=
    fun h => by simpa using congrFun h (Sum.inr 0)
  rw [twistedHatCoefficient_of_hatDomains_eq_pair
    (H.hatDomains_addBasepoint_zero_one_self hr₀ h₀) hne, one_def, ← ofAdd_zero]
  -- The crescent `C_β` has label `0` and the crescent `C_α` has label `C_α - C_β`.
  congr 3 <;> refine Subtype.ext ?_ <;> dsimp only <;>
    rw [ReferenceDomains.addBasepoint_label] <;> funext s <;> rcases s with s | m
  · simp
  · fin_cases m <;> simp
  · simp
  · fin_cases m <;> simp

variable {H} in
/-- **The Koszul coefficient `1 + t` at a weakly admissible generator.** If `r₀` contains a
basepoint and the diagram is weakly admissible at `x`, then the twisted coefficient of the diagram
with an added basepoint from `(x, 0)` to `(x, 1)` is `1 + t`. -/
theorem WeaklyAdmissibleAt.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self {x : H.Generator}
    (hW : H.WeaklyAdmissibleAt χ x) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) =
      1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1 :=
  H.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self hr₀ fun E hE hz hE₀ hμ =>
    weaklyAdmissibleAt_iff.mp hW E (isDomainBetween_self_iff.mp ⟨hE, hz⟩) hμ hE₀

/-- **No twisted coefficient from `p` to `q` between distinct generators.** Suppose that `r₀`
contains a basepoint and that the zero domain is the only nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero
from `x` to `y` avoiding the basepoints. If `x ≠ y`, the twisted coefficient of the diagram with an
added basepoint from `(x, 0)` to `(y, 1)` vanishes. -/
theorem twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_of_ne {x y : H.Generator}
    (h₀ : ∀ E, H.IsDomainBetween x y E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
      H.maslovIndex χ x y E = 0 → E = 0) (hxy : x ≠ y) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1) = 0 := by
  refine twistedHatCoefficient_eq_zero_of_hatDomains_eq_empty ?_
  rw [H.hatDomains_addBasepoint_zero_one r₀ hr₀ x y, Set.image_eq_empty, Set.prod_eq_empty_iff]
  exact Or.inl (Set.eq_empty_of_forall_notMem fun E hE =>
    hxy ((H.setOf_maslovIndex_eq_zero h₀ E).mp hE).1)

/-- **The twisted hat differential after adding a basepoint is a Koszul tensor product.** Suppose
that `r₀` contains a basepoint and that, for every generator `x`, the zero domain is the only
nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero from `x` to `y` avoiding the basepoints. Then the twisted
hat differential of the diagram with an added basepoint in `r₀` sends a chain `c` to the chain
whose coefficient at `(y, k)` is
`∑ₓ c(x, k) ι(c(x, y)) + [k = 1] (1 + t) c(y, 0)`, where `c(x, y)` are the twisted coefficients of
the original diagram, `ι` is `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRingHom` and `t` is
the monomial of the periodic domain `C_α - C_β`: the old twisted differential tensored with the
Koszul complex `p ↦ (1 + t) q`. -/
theorem twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply (y : H.Generator)
    (h₀ : ∀ x E, H.IsDomainBetween x y E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
      H.maslovIndex χ x y E = 0 → E = 0)
    (c : (H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (k : Fin 2) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) c
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y k) =
      (∑ x, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x k) *
        H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y)) +
        if k = 1 then c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0) *
          (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1)
        else 0 := by
  classical
  rw [twistedHatDifferential_apply, Finsupp.sum_fintype _ _ (by simp),
    ← (H.addBasepointGeneratorEquiv r₀).sum_comp, Fintype.sum_prod_type]
  simp only [addBasepointGeneratorEquiv_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  obtain rfl | rfl : k = 0 ∨ k = 1 := by omega
  · simp [twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_self H hr₀,
      twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_one_zero H hr₀]
  · have hcoef (x : H.Generator) :
        (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatCoefficient (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
          (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1) =
        if x = y then
          1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1
        else 0 := by
      split_ifs with hxy
      · subst hxy
        exact H.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_self hr₀ (h₀ _)
      · exact H.twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_zero_one_of_ne hr₀ (h₀ x) hxy
    simp only [hcoef, twistedHatCoefficient_addBasepoint_self H hr₀, mul_ite, mul_zero,
      Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_ite_eq', Finset.mem_univ, ite_true]
    exact add_comm _ _

end Hat

section Retraction

/-- The ring map from the group ring of the periodic domains of the diagram with an added basepoint
in `r₀` back to that of the original diagram, induced by the projection `(Q, m) ↦ Q` of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv`. It sends the monomial `t` of the
new periodic domain `C_α - C_β` to `1`, and it is a left inverse of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRingHom`. -/
noncomputable def addBasepointTwistedRetraction :
    MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains) →+*
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative H.periodicDomains) :=
  mapDomainRingHom (ZMod 2) (AddMonoidHom.toMultiplicative
    ((AddMonoidHom.fst _ _).comp (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀).symm.toAddMonoidHom))

/-- The retraction sends the monomial `t^{(Q, m)}` to the monomial `t^Q`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedRetraction_single (P : (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains)
    (a : ZMod 2) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀ (single (Multiplicative.ofAdd P) a) =
      single (Multiplicative.ofAdd ((H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀).symm P).1) a := by
  simp [addBasepointTwistedRetraction]

/-- The retraction is a left inverse of the inclusion of group rings
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRingHom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedRetraction_addBasepointTwistedRingHom
    (a : MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative H.periodicDomains)) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀ (H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ a) = a :=
  RingHom.congr_fun (TauCeti.MonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom_fst_comp_symm_comp_inl (ZMod 2)
    (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀)) a

/-- The retraction kills the Koszul coefficient `1 + t`: it sends `t` to `1`, and `1 + 1 = 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedRetraction_one_add_single :
    H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀
      (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1) = 0 := by
  simp [← one_def, ZModModule.add_self]

/-- **The kernel of the retraction is generated by `1 + t`.** Setting `t = 1` identifies the group
ring of the periodic domains of the diagram with an added basepoint, modulo `1 + t`, with the group
ring of the periodic domains of the original diagram. -/
theorem ker_addBasepointTwistedRetraction :
    RingHom.ker (H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀) =
      Ideal.span
        {1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1} := by
  rw [addBasepointTwistedRetraction, TauCeti.MonoidAlgebra.ker_mapDomainRingHom_fst_comp_symm,
    ZModModule.sub_eq_add, add_comm (single _ _)]

end Retraction

/-- Two chains of the diagram with an added basepoint are equal if they agree at the generators
`(y, 0)` and at the generators `(y, 1)`. -/
private theorem ext_addBasepointGenerator {M : Type*} [Zero M]
    {c c' : (H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀ M}
    (h0 : ∀ y, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0) = c' (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0))
    (h1 : ∀ y, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1) = c' (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1)) :
    c = c' := by
  refine Finsupp.ext fun g => ?_
  obtain ⟨⟨y, k⟩, rfl⟩ := H.addBasepointGenerator_surjective r₀ g
  obtain rfl | rfl : k = 0 ∨ k = 1 := by omega
  exacts [h0 y, h1 y]

section Homology

variable [Fintype Point]

/-- The chain map from the twisted hat complex of the diagram with an added basepoint in `r₀` to
that of the original diagram: it keeps the coefficients at the generators `(y, 1)` and sets `t` to
`1` in them, `c ↦ (y ↦ ε (c (y, 1)))`, where `ε` is
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedRetraction`. It is semilinear along `ε`. -/
noncomputable def addBasepointTwistedProjection :
    ((H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains)) →ₛₗ[
        H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀]
      H.Generator →₀ MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative H.periodicDomains) where
  toFun c := Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm fun y =>
    H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀ (c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1))
  map_add' c c' := by ext; simp
  map_smul' a c := by ext; simp

/-- The projection reads the coefficient at `(y, 1)` with `t` set to `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedProjection_apply (c : (H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (y : H.Generator) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀ c y =
      H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀ (c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1)) := by
  simp [addBasepointTwistedProjection]

variable [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region] {χ : Region → ℤ} {r : H.ReferenceDomains} {r₀}
  (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)

/-- The coefficient form of `∂ ∘ ∂ = 0` for the twisted hat differential `∂` of the original
diagram, with coefficients pushed into the larger group ring. -/
private theorem sum_sum_mul_addBasepointTwistedRingHom_eq_zero
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0)
    (f : H.Generator → MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (y : H.Generator) :
    ∑ x, (∑ z, f z * H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ z x)) *
      H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) = 0 := by
  simp_rw [Finset.sum_mul, mul_assoc]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm]
  simp_rw [← Finset.mul_sum, ← map_mul, ← map_sum,
    H.sum_twistedHatCoefficient_mul_twistedHatCoefficient_eq_zero hd, map_zero, mul_zero,
    Finset.sum_const_zero]

variable (h₀ : ∀ x y E, H.IsDomainBetween x y E → (∀ z, E (H.basepoint z) = 0) → 0 ≤ E →
  H.maslovIndex χ x y E = 0 → E = 0)
include h₀

/-- The coefficient at `(y, 0)` of the twisted hat differential after adding a basepoint. -/
private theorem twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_zero
    (c : (H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (y : H.Generator) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) c
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0) =
      ∑ x, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) *
        H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) := by
  simp [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply H hr₀ y (h₀ · y)]

/-- The coefficient at `(y, 1)` of the twisted hat differential after adding a basepoint. -/
private theorem twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_one
    (c : (H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (y : H.Generator) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) c
        (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1) =
      ∑ x, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) *
          H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) +
        c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 0) *
          (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1) := by
  simp [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply H hr₀ y (h₀ · y)]

/-- **The twisted hat differential after adding a basepoint squares to zero** if the original one
does. Suppose that `r₀` contains a basepoint and that the zero domain is the only nonnegative
domain of Maslov index zero between two generators avoiding the basepoints, so that the new
differential is the old one tensored with the Koszul complex of `1 + t`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply`). The cross terms
`(1 + t) ∂` and `∂ (1 + t)` cancel in characteristic two. -/
theorem twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) ∘ₗ
      (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) =
        0 := by
  have hA := H.sum_sum_mul_addBasepointTwistedRingHom_eq_zero (r₀ := r₀) hd
  refine LinearMap.ext fun c => H.ext_addBasepointGenerator r₀ (fun y => ?_) fun y => ?_ <;>
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply, Finsupp.zero_apply,
      twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_zero H hr₀ h₀,
      twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_one H hr₀ h₀]
  · exact hA _ y
  · -- The cross terms `(1 + t) ∂` and `∂ (1 + t)` are equal, so they cancel in characteristic two.
    have hcross : ∑ x, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) *
          (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1) *
          H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) =
        (∑ x, c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 0) *
          H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y)) *
          (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1) := by
      rw [Finset.sum_mul]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => mul_right_comm _ _ _
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => add_mul _ _ _, Finset.sum_add_distrib, hA, zero_add,
      hcross, ZModModule.add_self]

/-- **The projection is a chain map.** Under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply`, the projection
`c ↦ (y ↦ ε (c (y, 1)))` intertwines the twisted hat differentials: the Koszul term
`(1 + t) c(y, 0)` is killed by `ε`. -/
theorem addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential :
    H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀ ∘ₛₗ
        (H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀) (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) =
      H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₛₗ H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀ := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun c => Finsupp.ext fun y => ?_
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, addBasepointTwistedProjection_apply,
    twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply H hr₀ y (h₀ · y), twistedHatDifferential_apply_eq_sum]
  simp [addBasepointTwistedRetraction_one_add_single]

/-- A cycle `c` of the new twisted complex whose projection is a boundary `∂ w` is a boundary:
subtracting the boundary of `(0, w)` leaves a multiple `v (1 + t)` at the generators `(y, 1)`, and
`c` is the boundary of `(v, w)`, since `1 + t` is not a zero divisor. -/
private theorem homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_injective
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0) :
    Injective (LinearMap.homologyMap (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀)
      (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd) hd
      (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential hr₀ h₀)) := by
  set u : MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains) :=
    1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) 1 with hu_def
  have hu : u ≠ 0 := one_add_single_ne_zero (by simp) _
  rw [LinearMap.homologyMap_injective_iff]
  rintro c hc ⟨w, hw⟩
  have hn (y : H.Generator) : c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1) -
      ∑ x, H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (w x) *
        H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ x y) ∈ Ideal.span {u} := by
    rw [hu_def, ← ker_addBasepointTwistedRetraction, RingHom.mem_ker]
    have := congr($hw y)
    simp only [twistedHatDifferential_apply_eq_sum, addBasepointTwistedProjection_apply] at this
    simp [map_sub, map_sum, map_mul, ← this]
  choose v hv using fun y => Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 (hn y)
  refine ⟨(H.addBasepointChainProdEquiv r₀).symm (Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm v,
      Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm fun x => H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (w x)),
    H.ext_addBasepointGenerator r₀ (fun y => ?_) fun y => ?_⟩
  · simp only [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_zero H hr₀ h₀,
      addBasepointChainProdEquiv_symm_apply_zero, Finsupp.coe_equivFunOnFinite_symm]
    -- Cancel the factor `1 + t`, which is not a zero divisor.
    refine (IsRegular.of_ne_zero' hu).right ?_
    dsimp only
    have h1 := congr($hc (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ y 1))
    simp only [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_one H hr₀ h₀, Finsupp.coe_zero,
      Pi.zero_apply] at h1
    have hc1 (x : H.Generator) : c (H.addBasepointGenerator r₀ x 1) = v x * u +
        ∑ z, H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (w z) *
          H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (H.twistedHatCoefficient r χ z x) := by
      rw [hv x]; abel
    simp_rw [hc1, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib,
      H.sum_sum_mul_addBasepointTwistedRingHom_eq_zero hd, add_zero] at h1
    rw [← (eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left h1).trans (ZModModule.neg_eq_self _), Finset.sum_mul]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => mul_right_comm _ _ _
  · simp only [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_one H hr₀ h₀,
      addBasepointChainProdEquiv_symm_apply_one, addBasepointChainProdEquiv_symm_apply_zero,
      Finsupp.coe_equivFunOnFinite_symm]
    rw [hv y]; abel

/-- A cycle `z` of the original twisted complex is the projection of the cycle `(0, z)` of the new
one. -/
private theorem homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_surjective
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0) :
    Surjective (LinearMap.homologyMap (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀)
      (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd) hd
      (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential hr₀ h₀)) := by
  rw [LinearMap.homologyMap_surjective_iff]
  intro z hz
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker] at hz
  refine ⟨(H.addBasepointChainProdEquiv r₀).symm
    (0, Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm fun x => H.addBasepointTwistedRingHom r₀ (z x)), ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]
    refine H.ext_addBasepointGenerator r₀ (fun y => ?_) fun y => ?_
    · simp [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_zero H hr₀ h₀]
    · simp only [twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply_one H hr₀ h₀,
        addBasepointChainProdEquiv_symm_apply_one, addBasepointChainProdEquiv_symm_apply_zero,
        Finsupp.coe_equivFunOnFinite_symm, Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply, zero_mul, add_zero]
      simp_rw [← map_mul, ← map_sum, ← twistedHatDifferential_apply_eq_sum, hz, Finsupp.coe_zero,
        Pi.zero_apply, map_zero]
  · convert (LinearMap.range (H.twistedHatDifferential r χ)).zero_mem
    rw [sub_eq_zero]
    ext y
    simp

/-- **Adding a basepoint does not change the twisted homology.** Suppose that `r₀` contains a
basepoint, that the zero domain is the only nonnegative domain of Maslov index zero between two
generators avoiding the basepoints, and that the twisted hat differential of the original diagram
squares to zero. Then the projection `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedProjection`
induces a bijection from the twisted homology of the diagram with an added basepoint onto that of
the original diagram.

The new complex is the mapping cone of multiplication by `1 + t` on the old complex with
coefficients in the larger group ring. Since `1 + t` is not a zero divisor, the cone computes the
homology of the quotient by `1 + t`, which is the old complex: setting `t = 1` is the retraction,
whose kernel is generated by `1 + t`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.ker_addBasepointTwistedRetraction`). -/
theorem homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_bijective
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0) :
    Bijective (LinearMap.homologyMap (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀)
      (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd) hd
      (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential hr₀ h₀)) :=
  ⟨H.homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_injective hr₀ h₀ hd,
    H.homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_surjective hr₀ h₀ hd⟩

/-- **The twisted homology after adding a basepoint**, under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_apply` and when the twisted hat
differential of the original diagram squares to zero: the twisted homology of the diagram with an
added basepoint is that of the original diagram, through the map induced by
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedProjection`. The group ring of the new periodic
domains acts through the retraction `t ↦ 1`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_smul`). -/
noncomputable def addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0) :
    ((H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀)
        (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)).homology
        (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd) ≃+
      (H.twistedHatDifferential r χ).homology hd :=
  AddEquiv.ofBijective _ (H.homologyMap_addBasepointTwistedProjection_bijective hr₀ h₀ hd)

/-- The equivalence sends the class of a cycle `c` to the class of its projection
`y ↦ ε (c (y, 1))`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_mk
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0)
    (c : LinearMap.ker ((H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀)
      (addBasepointEuler χ r₀))) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv hr₀ h₀ hd (Submodule.Quotient.mk c) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀ c,
        LinearMap.map_mem_ker_of_comp_eq _
          (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential hr₀ h₀) c.property⟩ := by
  rw [addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv, AddEquiv.ofBijective_apply]
  exact LinearMap.homologyMap_mk _ _ _ _ c

/-- **The coefficients act through the retraction.** An element `a` of the group ring of the
periodic domains of the diagram with an added basepoint acts on its twisted homology as its
retraction `ε a` acts on the twisted homology of the original diagram. -/
theorem addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_smul
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0)
    (a : MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains))
    (z : ((H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀)
        (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)).homology
        (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd)) :
    H.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv hr₀ h₀ hd (a • z) =
      H.addBasepointTwistedRetraction r₀ a • H.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv hr₀ h₀ hd z :=
  map_smulₛₗ (LinearMap.homologyMap (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection r₀) _ hd
    (H.addBasepointTwistedProjection_comp_twistedHatDifferential hr₀ h₀)) a z

/-- **`1 + t` annihilates the twisted homology after adding a basepoint**: the class of the sphere
around the new basepoint acts trivially. -/
theorem addBasepoint_one_add_single_smul_eq_zero
    (hd : H.twistedHatDifferential r χ ∘ₗ H.twistedHatDifferential r χ = 0)
    (z : ((H.addBasepoint r₀).twistedHatDifferential (r.addBasepoint hr₀)
        (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)).homology
        (H.twistedHatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ h₀ hd)) :
    (1 + single (Multiplicative.ofAdd (H.addBasepointPeriodicDomainsEquiv r₀ (0, 1))) (1 : ZMod 2) :
      MonoidAlgebra (ZMod 2) (Multiplicative (H.addBasepoint r₀).periodicDomains)) • z = 0 := by
  apply (H.addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv hr₀ h₀ hd).injective
  rw [addBasepointTwistedHomologyEquiv_smul, addBasepointTwistedRetraction_one_add_single,
    zero_smul, map_zero]

